              "title": "Sean Carroll, Lecture Notes on General Relativity, complete lecture notes, Ch. 3 \u00a73.3",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/gr-qc/9712019"
            }
          ]
        },
        "physical_scope": "Classical spinless structureless point test body of constant primitive mass m>0 on a prescribed smooth background; no self-field, radiation reaction, finite-size, quantum, or global-completeness claim.",
        "library": "physics"
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-rpm-einbein-variation-and-equivalence",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Positive-einbein variation and massive/null sector equations",
        "statement": "Let $a<b$, let $x:[a,b]\\to M$ be a $C^2$ curve with parameter $s$ and $T=dx/ds$, fix $c>0$, let $e(s)>0$ be smooth, and let $m\\ge0$ be constant. Take independent $C^2$ fixed-endpoint variations of $x$ and smooth interior variations of $e$. For the action\n\n$$S_e[x,e]=\\frac12\\int_a^b\\!\\left(e^{-1}g(T,T)-em^2c^2\\right)ds,$$\n\nindependent fixed-endpoint variations in $x$ and interior variations in $e$ give\n\n$$g(T,T)+e^2m^2c^2=0,\\qquad D_s(T/e)=0.$$\n\nOn the future timelike massive branch $m>0$, this constraint uniquely gives $e=\\ell/(mc)$, $T/e=mU$, and the action reduces to $-mc\\int\\ell ds$; in proper-time gauge $s=\\tau$, $e=1/m$. On the nonzero future null branch $m=0$, $P:=T/e$ is nonzero future null and $D_sP=0$; if $d\\lambda=e\\,ds$, then $dx/d\\lambda=P$ and $D_\\lambda P=0$. There is no null proper-time gauge, and the scale of $P$ remains initial data. For finite intervals $[a',b']$ and $[a,b]$, an orientation-preserving $C^\\infty$ diffeomorphism $s=\\phi(r):[a',b']\\to[a,b]$ with $\\phi'(r)>0$ gives $T_r(r)=\\phi'(r)T(\\phi(r))$ and $e_r(r)=\\phi'(r)e(\\phi(r))$; the einbein action is invariant, and this transformation preserves the stated $C^2$ curve and smooth-einbein configuration class.",
        "deps": [
          "def-rpm-spacetime-observer-and-worldline",
          "thm-rpm-proper-time-parametrization",
          "lem-rpm-length-action-first-variation",
          "thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative",
