      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-free-massive-and-null-geodesics",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Free massive and null particle geodesics",
        "statement": "On a prescribed smooth time-oriented Lorentzian background, stationarity for the massive action of [[post-rpm-massive-test-particle-action]] is defined on a finite segment $[a,b]$ with the stated fixed-endpoint $C^2$ variations. A stationary massive path on that segment satisfies $D_\\tau U=0$ in proper-time parameter, with $P=mU$ and $m>0$ constant. In the separately adopted null sector of [[post-rpm-null-test-particle-action]], stationarity for the einbein action is likewise defined on a finite segment, using independent fixed-endpoint $C^2$ variations of the curve and smooth interior variations of the einbein. Its nonzero future-null branch has momentum $P$ satisfying $D_\\lambda P=0$ in an affine parameter $\\lambda$ with $dx/d\\lambda=P$. These equations hold locally on the interiors of the finite segments; their ODE solutions extend uniquely to maximal solutions on open intervals, with no action integrated over an infinite interval. For any $\\tau_0\\in\\mathbb R$ and $p_0\\in M$, an initial vector $U_0\\in T_{p_0}M$ that is future timelike and satisfies $g_{p_0}(U_0,U_0)=-c^2$ determines a unique local massive solution with $x(\\tau_0)=p_0$, $U(\\tau_0)=U_0$, and a unique maximal solution on an open interval containing $\\tau_0$. For any $\\lambda_0\\in\\mathbb R$ and $p_0\\in M$, a nonzero future-null vector $P_0\\in T_{p_0}M$ determines a unique local null solution with $x(\\lambda_0)=p_0$, $P(\\lambda_0)=P_0$, and a unique maximal solution on an open interval containing $\\lambda_0$. Neither maximal interval is asserted to be all of $\\mathbb R$.\n\nMore explicitly, there are open intervals $J\\ni\\tau_0$ and $J'\\ni\\lambda_0$ such that the massive local solution is a $C^2$ curve $x:J\\to M$ with $U=dx/d\\tau$, and the null local solution is a $C^2$ curve $x:J'\\to M$ with $P=dx/d\\lambda$; their stated initial values are imposed at the indicated parameter values.",
        "deps": [
          "post-rpm-massive-test-particle-action",
          "post-rpm-null-test-particle-action",
          "def-rpm-mechanical-momentum-and-observer-energy",
          "lem-rpm-length-action-first-variation",
          "lem-rpm-einbein-variation-and-equivalence",
          "thm-rpm-proper-time-parametrization",
          "thm-gr-local-geodesics-and-exponential-map"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
