      {
        "id": "post-rpm-prescribed-force-law",
        "kind": "postulate",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Prescribed constant-mass force law",
        "statement": "For a named massive test body with constant primitive mass $m>0$ measured in kilograms, SI conversion constant $c>0$ in metres per second, and momentum $P=mU$ as defined in [[def-rpm-mechanical-momentum-and-observer-energy]], define the future unit timelike shell by\n\n$$\\Sigma_c^+:=\\{(p,V)\\in TM:V\\text{ future timelike},\\ g_p(V,V)=-c^2\\}.$$\n\nLet $\\mathcal V\\subset TM$ be an open neighborhood of $\\Sigma_c^+$ contained in the future timelike velocity cone. For a massive body trajectory $x:I\\to M$ that is $C^2$ and parameterized by proper time $\\tau$, with $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ a nonempty open interval, put $U=dx/d\\tau$ and require $(x(\\tau),U(\\tau))\\in\\Sigma_c^+\\subseteq\\mathcal V$ for every $\\tau\\in I$. Specify a smooth map $f:\\mathcal V\\to TM$ over the bundle projection $\\pi:TM\\to M$, meaning $\\pi(f(p,V))=p$ (equivalently, $f(p,V)\\in T_pM$), and require $g_p(V,f(p,V))=0$ for every $(p,V)\\in\\mathcal V$. One may adopt this force map and the equation\n\n$$D_\\tau P=f(x,U).$$\n\nThe orthogonality condition is part of this model's compatibility assumptions, imposed throughout $\\mathcal V$; it preserves $g(U,U)=-c^2$ for constant $m$. Since $P=mU$, this equation is equivalent to $D_\\tau U=f(x,U)/m$ on the stated domain. It is not a law selecting a force for every particle or interaction. A local IVP follows only for data in $\\mathcal V$, as in [[lem-rpm-shell-tangent-force-ivp]]. The force has SI units newtons when $\\tau$ is in seconds and $P$ has units kg m s$^{-1}$. No empirical force measurements, universal coupling, or global existence are asserted.",
        "deps": [
          "def-rpm-mechanical-momentum-and-observer-energy",
          "lem-rpm-shell-tangent-force-ivp"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-rpm-mechanical-momentum-and-observer-energy": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "lem-rpm-shell-tangent-force-ivp": "formulation-prerequisite"
        },
