        },
        "strategy": "direct",
        "physical_scope": "Conditional scalar balance for a test particle and a specified Killing field; energy interpretation only for a future unit time-translation field, with no global symmetry assumption.",
        "library": "physics",
        "proof_strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-mass-shell-and-force-work",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Mass shell, observer energy and inertial work",
        "statement": "For a massive body with constant $m>0$, $P=mU$, $g(U,U)=-c^2$, and the force law of [[post-rpm-prescribed-force-law]],\n\n$$g(P,P)=-m^2c^2.$$\n\nFor every observer $n$ at the event, the energy and spatial momentum defined in [[def-rpm-mechanical-momentum-and-observer-energy]] satisfy\n\n$$E_n(P)^2=m^2c^4+c^2g(q_n(P),q_n(P)),\\qquad E_n(P)>0.$$\n\nFor a nonzero future-null $P$, $E_n(P)=c\\sqrt{g(q_n(P),q_n(P))}$. In a flat inertial frame $(o;e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3)$ with $n=e_0$ and inertial chart $x^0=ct$ from [[def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart]], let $E=E_n(P)$, let $\\mathbf p$ be the spatial coordinates of $q_n(P)$ in $(e_1,e_2,e_3)$, set $\\mathbf v=d\\mathbf x/dt$, and define $\\mathbf F=d\\mathbf p/dt$. Then $dE/dt=\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf v$ under the constant-mass force hypotheses. If $m(\\tau)>0$ is $C^1$, $U$ is $C^1$ with $g(U,U)=-c^2$, and $P=m(\\tau)U$, then the kinematic identity $g(U,D_\\tau P)=-c^2\\dot m$ holds; it specifies no variable-mass law.",
        "deps": [
          "post-rpm-prescribed-force-law",
          "lem-rpm-shell-tangent-force-ivp",
          "def-rpm-mechanical-momentum-and-observer-energy",
