      {
        "id": "ex-rpm-clock-reunion",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Ideal-clock readings for a flat reunion path",
        "statement": "Choose an inertial frame $(o;e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3)$ and its inertial chart $\\chi$ from [[def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart]], with coordinates $(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)=(ct,x,y,z)$. Let $T>0$ seconds and $0<v<c$. A lab clock has chart path $\\chi\\circ x_L(t)=(ct,0,0,0)$ for $0\\le t\\le2T$. A traveler has chart path $\\chi\\circ x_R(t)=(ct,vt,0,0)$ on $[0,T]$ and $\\chi\\circ x_R(t)=(ct,v(2T-t),0,0)$ on $[T,2T]$. The traveler reverses direction at $t=T$ and reunites with the lab at $t=2T$.",
        "deps": [
          "post-rpm-test-clock-and-background",
          "thm-rpm-proper-time-parametrization",
          "def-gr-timelike-worldline-and-proper-time",
